+Aegis — 2‑Week Hardening Checklist: Federated Learning (Flower) + Secure Aggregation + HSM
+
+Goal
+- Harden the Flower FL control plane and client onboarding for production: TLS + auth, minimal RBAC/NetworkPolicy, DP tuning, secure aggregation evaluation, and HSM signing & rotation readiness.
+- Two-week execution with clear owners and exit criteria.
+
+Assumptions / prerequisites
+- Kubernetes cluster (staging) with cert-manager installed OR permission to install.
+- Vault running and operator has VAULT_TOKEN.
+- MLflow tracking server reachable with credentials.
+- Cosign key reference prepared and accessible to ops (KMS/COSIGN_KEY_REF).
+- Operator account with permissions to manage CloudHSM/KMS.
+
+Week 0 / Preparation (pre‑work, 1–2 days)
+- Owner: Platform / Crypto
+- Tasks:
+  - Confirm cert-manager installed (v1.8+ recommended) and ingress controller (ingress-nginx / contour).
+  - Gather OAuth provider details (client id/secret, redirect URLs) for oauth2-proxy (or plan for an OIDC provider).
+  - Ensure cosign key ref available in Vault or KMS; verify cosign CLI can sign locally.
+  - Create namespace "aegis" in staging.
+- Exit criteria:
+  - cert-manager and ingress present.
+  - OAuth client ready (or plan to use static auth for staging).
+  - COSIGN_KEY_REF and MLFLOW creds available as Kubernetes secrets.
+
+Sprint Week 1 (Days 1–5) — Network & Auth (priority)
+- Owner: Platform / Security
+- Day 1:
+  - Apply RBAC and NetworkPolicy manifests (services/fl/secure/rbac-restricted.yaml, services/fl/secure/networkpolicy.yaml).
+  - Create K8s secrets:
+    - aegis-core-secrets: keys: COSIGN_KEY_REF, MLFLOW_DB_URL, EVIDENCE_BUCKET, OAUTH_COOKIE_SECRET (for oauth2-proxy).
+  - Exit: Flower service account cannot read cluster-wide secrets; secrets are scoped.
+- Day 2:
+  - Deploy oauth2-proxy (services/fl/secure/oauth2-proxy-deployment.yaml). Configure env from secret (OAUTH client id/secret).
+  - Deploy Flower (services/fl/k8s_deploy_flower.yaml) but keep ServiceClusterIP internal.
+  - Exit: oauth2-proxy reachable within cluster; Flower accessible only via oauth2-proxy.
+- Day 3:
+  - Create cert-manager ClusterIssuer & Certificate (services/fl/secure/clusterissuer-selfsigned.yaml, services/fl/secure/flower-certificate.yaml) or use a trusted CA for staging.
+  - Deploy Ingress with TLS (services/fl/secure/flower-ingress.yaml) protecting path with oauth2-proxy integration.
+  - Exit: TLS termination works; browser/API client can access via Ingress and gets authenticated.
+- Day 4–5:
+  - Penetration quick-check: verify Flower endpoint is not publicly accessible without OAuth token; validate NetworkPolicy denies other namespaces.
+  - Document ingress domain and TLS cert secret name.
+  - Exit: Security smoke-pass.
+
+Sprint Week 2 (Days 6–10) — DP, secure aggregation evaluation & HSM drill
+- Owner: ML Eng / Crypto / Platform
+- Day 6:
+  - DP testing: run FL privacy smoke (.github/workflows/fl_security_and_dp.yml) on staging; tune Opacus noise and sample rate parameters.
+  - Exit: Determine epsilon target and noise multiplier that balance utility / privacy.
+- Day 7:
+  - Secure aggregation evaluation: spin up research session to test PySyft/CrypTen prototypes; run sample secure aggregation scaffold (services/fl/secure_agg_pysyft_scaffold.py).
+  - Exit: Decision: (A) rely on DP only, or (B) integrate cryptographic aggregator (timeline).
+- Day 8:
+  - HSM rotation drill (ops/hsm/aws_hsm_activation_and_rotation_drill.sh): run dry-run, record issuance manifest, validate cosign operation with KMS.
+  - Exit: Documented rotation steps and evidence bucket integration.
+- Day 9:
+  - Integrate MLflow register/sign: run full FL round (demo) and register model via ops/fl/aggregate_and_register.py; cosign sign artifact; save manifest to evidence bucket.
+  - Exit: Model artifact cryptographically signed and evidence stored.
+- Day 10:
+  - Post-mortem and runbook updates: update docs/runbooks with exact commands, recoveries, and who to call on incidents.
+  - Exit: Sign-off from Security and Crypto.
+
+Deliverables & Acceptance Criteria (end of 2 weeks)
+- Flower behind TLS + OIDC/OAuth2 via oauth2-proxy, with ClusterIssuer certificate.
+- NetworkPolicy and RBAC limiting access to Flower and secrets.
+- FL clients enrolled in staging and DP parameters chosen; privacy smoke run completes.
+- Decision recorded re: cryptographic secure aggregation; if yes, plan created.
+- HSM rotation drill run (dry-run) and cosign signing demonstrated for FL artifact.
+- Runbook updated with commands and owners.
+
+Follow-ups (post 2 weeks)
+- Implement automated client enrollment & attestation for edge devices.
+- Integrate secure aggregator (if chosen) and run larger scale FL jobs.
+- Full production hardening: service mesh mtls, OPA/Gatekeeper policies, KMS/HSM redundancy, insurer/auditor acceptance.
+
+````
